15 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Map of the British Isles and surrounding waters with bathymetric variations indicated by color. Areas are divided into sections IV-a, IV-b, and IV-c, outlined in red and black dashed lines. Depths range from greater than negative seven hundred meters to more than fifty meters, represented by colors from deep purple to bright yellow. Red triangles mark specific locations. Latitude and longitude lines provide geographic context.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Comparison diagram of two ecosystem models from the 1990s and 1890s, showing identical topologies. Both models display network diagrams with nodes connected by lines, indicating ecosystem interactions. The right side lists variables such as Biomass, Production/Biomass, Consumption/Biomass, Ecotrophic Efficiency, Diet Composition, and Catches, linking to Natural Mortality, P/Q, EE, and Diet Composition. Dashed lines differentiate applicability to all or specific groups. The text \215Identical topologies! Balancing together\216 emphasizes model similarities.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Two network diagrams compare marine food webs from the 1890s and 1990s. Both diagrams display trophic levels from one to five. Nodes represent species or groups, with lines indicating interactions. Notable connections include phytoplankton, zooplankton, and detritus at the base, leading to a range of fish, marine mammals, and fisheries. The overall structure appears densely interconnected.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Flow diagram showing trophic levels with five compartments labeled P, II, III, IV, and V. Each box contains figures for consumption, biomass, respiration, and more. Arrows indicate the flow between compartments, including flow to detritus. Details on catch, trophic efficiency, predation, and respiration are shown in the lower panel.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Heatmap displaying mutual trophic impacts \(MTI\) between various marine species and fisheries. Rows and columns are labeled with species and fisheries, respectively. Colors range from purple \(positive impact\) to red \(negative impact\) with a scale from -1 to 1. Notable red and purple squares indicate significant interactions.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot comparing keystoneness and relative total impact of species in ECS_1890s and ECS_1990s models. Circular markers represent species, sized by impact, with ECS_1890s in green and ECS_1990s in orange. Species are labeled numerically, corresponding to a list, including phytoplankton, zooplankton, and cetaceans.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
